# Frontend Standards

## Next.js App Router

- Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only for interactivity (state, effects, event handlers)
- Use `loading.tsx` and `error.tsx` for route-level loading/error states
- Data fetching in Server Components via `fetch` with proper cache/revalidation settings

## Component Library

Use **shadcn/ui** as the component foundation. Never build from scratch what shadcn provides (Button, Dialog, Card, Input, Tabs, etc.). Customize via Tailwind classes and the `cn()` utility.

## API Client

All backend calls go through `lib/api.ts` -- a typed client with:
- Base URL from environment variable `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`
- Typed request/response generics
- Error handling wrapper

```typescript
export async function fetchBooks(): Promise<Book[]> {
  const res = await fetch(`${API_URL}/books`);
  if (!res.ok) throw new ApiError(res.status, await res.text());
  return res.json();
}
```

## Streaming Chat

Use SSE (`EventSource` or `fetch` with `ReadableStream`) for chat responses. Parse streamed tokens and render incrementally with markdown support.

## Styling

- Mobile-first: base styles for mobile, `md:` and `lg:` for larger screens
- Use Tailwind utility classes; avoid custom CSS files
- Dark mode support via `dark:` variants and CSS variables

## Accessibility

- Semantic HTML (`<main>`, `<nav>`, `<article>`, `<section>`)
- ARIA labels on interactive elements without visible text
- Keyboard navigation for all interactive components
- Focus management for modals and dynamic content
